ot  good offensive players this offensive  line was as good as Dallas two years ago  now I don't know what's happened to it  and and what he wants but I think they  are building for the future that's the  game plan but those draft choices can be  iffy you know there's no guarantee all  Ryan Leaf was supposed to be a savior  and it didn't turn out to be that way  and we've all seen it  Andre Bruce and you know you can go on  down the line there's no guarantee  because you got three number one draft  choice they're all gonna be great player  do you feel like you won two Super Bowls  I know they know I don't I really don't  I've heard  people say that all the time and I  really don't Jim Mora laid a great  foundation for me in Indianapolis when  when we got there those guys knew how to  work the offense was in place several  the offensive coaches were there Peyton  Manning was there  those guys were more ready to go it took  us a little while to do it but you know  everything is different John put his  system in day one they did a great job  and you have to tip your head to that  and that's what he's trying to do in  Oakland and we'll see what happens  here's a question that we brought up we  had Roger Staubach on in the first hour  and I Paulie said whose career would you  rather have Rodgers or Terry Bradshaw's  I think I'd rather have Terry Bradshaw I  mean Roger was outstanding for a long  time now you get college - you get the  Heisman Trophy - I'm still taking the  fourth Superbowl away okay you know  terry has the ups and down getting best  Roger had some of that too you know  alternating with Craig Morton and  through the quarterback action some of  the injuries and things and he was  tremendous but I think that Terry  Bradshaw going from 70 to 279 and that  10-year stretch went in for Super Bowls  and playing with all those great players  I think I'd take that one and I was  trying to explain this that if you saw  Roger when he played he came in at age  27 but his style of play  could you imagine in him in today where  you have the rpoS here I don't because I  don't remember a quarterback you know  Fran Tarkenton scrambled but Roger beats  you with his legs like he would make you  pay when he scrambled he'd run for a  first down where Fran just was keeping a  play alive I don't know I don't remember  another quarterback who was like that at  that time in the NFL before Roger  Staubach I mean maybe you can help no he  was unique and a tremendous athlete and  that desire in Wilderland but if he had  this type of system where you could  create and where they couldn't really  hit you he would be very hard to deal  with tone good to talk to you have a  good weekend hope the kids are good and  we'll be watching Sunday night all right  thank you buddy  that's a Tony Dungy football night in  America Continental Tire Coaches Corner  Continental Tire proud to be supportive  the Dan Patrick show no matter what you  drive where you drive how you drive  continental as a tire for you  Continental Tire shares your passion for  the game show them your passion by  tweeting your photos to at Continental  Tire for more information visit  Continental Tire dot-com for more Dan  Patrick show to the audience Channel 239  on DirecTV or download the Dan Patrick  show at  [Music]

